{"conflicting_accesses": [{"first_access": "Write of size 4 at 0x5555569e66c0 by thread T1", "second_access": "Previous read of size 4 at 0x5555569e66c0 by thread T2", "observed_evidence": "ThreadSanitizer: data race (pid=10) on memory location 0x5555569e66c0 (right) in update_pair and snapshot_ok; T1 writes right = -n after unlocking guard, T2 reads right during snapshot_ok; both access right without mutual exclusion, despite guard being held in update_pair only for left assignment."}], "missing_synchronization": "The write to 'right' in update_pair is not protected by the mutex; the mutex is released after writing 'left' and reacquired before writing 'right', leaving a window where 'right' is accessible without synchronization. The read in snapshot_ok is unprotected, violating mutual exclusion with concurrent writes.", "invariant_to_preserve": "The invariant a + b == 0 in snapshot_ok must hold for all consistent snapshots; this requires that both 'left' and 'right' be read atomically under the same mutex, and that updates to both fields be atomic under the same mutex.", "edits": [{"file": "solution.c", "search": "void update_pair(int n) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&guard);
    left = n;
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&guard);
    sched_yield();
    pthread_mutex_lock(&guard);
    right = -n;
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&guard);
}", "replacement": "void update_pair(int n) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&guard);
    left = n;
    right = -n;
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&guard);
}"}]}
